sizingMode flags remain as set. If hugP=true then resize width would be overridden... I set sizing before resize; if hug, skip resize. Let me handle: only resize for dims when corresponding sizing is FIXED.\n\nActually simpler: for vertical stacks: primary axis = vertical (height), counter = horizontal (width). hugP → primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' (height hugs). hugC → counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO' (width hugs). For width fixed: counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize(w, anything). Height fixed: primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize.\n\nBut layoutGrow for children: child.layoutGrow=1 (in horizontal parent grows width).\n\nI'll write per-case explicitly rather than one clever helper — more code but safer. Let me still use helper but carefully.\n\nIcon ids map:\n```js\nconst ICONS={Back:'2:2',Bill:'2:3',Car:'2:4',ChevDown:'2:5',ChevRight:'2:6',More:'2:7',Offers:'2:8',Overview:'2:9',Plus:'2:10',Setting:'2:11',ThisMonth:'2:12'};\nconst LOGOS={Apple:'2:13',Netflix:'2:14',Patreon:'2:15',Spotify:'2:16'};\nfunction recolor(node,color){const vs=node.findAll(n=>n.type==='VECTOR');for(const v of vs){if(v.strokes&&v.strokes.length)v.strokes=[solid(color)];}}\nasync function icon(key,color,size){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(ICONS[key]);const i=c.createInstance();i.name='Icon_'+key;recolor(i,color);if(size&&size!==24)i.rescale(size/24);return i;}\nasync function logo(key,scale){const c=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(LOGOS[key]);const i=c.createInstance();i.name='Logo';if(scale&&scale!==1)i.rescale(scale);return i;}\n```\n\nTabBar:\n```js\nconst tb=figma.createComponent();tb.name='Tab Bar';tb.x=1550;tb.y=0;\ntb.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';tb.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED';tb.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';tb.resize(375,80);\ntb.primaryAxisAlignItems='SPACE_BETWEEN';tb.counterAxisAlignItems='MIN';tb.paddingLeft=30;tb.paddingRight=30;tb.paddingTop=13;\ntb.fills=[solid(C.surface)];tb.strokes=[solid(C.line)];tb.strokeTopWeight=1;tb.strokeLeftWeight=0;tb.strokeRightWeight=0;tb.strokeBottomWeight=0;tb.strokeAlign='INSIDE';\nconst tabs=[['Overview','Overview',false],['This Month','ThisMonth',true],['Offers','Offers',false],['Setting','Setting',false]];\nfor(const [label,key,active] of tabs){\n  const col=stack('VERTICAL',5,{hugP:true,hugC:true,align:'CENTER'});col.name='Tab / '+label;\n  col.appendChild(await icon(key,active?C.brand:C.ink3,24));\n  col.appendChild(txt(label,11,active?'SemiBold':'Medium',active?C.brand:C.ink3,{ls:0.2,center:true}));\n  tb.appendChild(col);\n}\n```\nWait stack with both hug: resize skipped ✓.\n\nNote: Tab item spacing in space-between with padding 30: items at edges; Overview label left-ish. iOS tab bars space items evenly across full width — acceptable.\n\nHeader component:\n```js\nconst hd=figma.createComponent();hd.name='Header';hd.x=1550;hd.y=120;\nhd.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';hd.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED';hd.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';hd.resize(375,52);\nhd.primaryAxisAlignItems='SPACE_BETWEEN';hd.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';hd.paddingLeft=16;hd.paddingRight=16;hd.fills=[];\nconst left=stack('HORIZONTAL',12,{hugP:true,hugC:true,align:'CENTER'});left.name='Left';\nleft.appendChild(await icon('Back',C.ink,24));\nconst title=txt('Expenses',16,'SemiBold',C.ink,{name:'Title'});\nleft.appendChild(title);hd.appendChild(left);\nconst plus=await icon('Plus',C.ink,24);plus.name='Plus';hd.appendChild(plus);\n```\n\nSegment:\n```js\nconst seg=figma.createComponent();seg.name='Segmented Control';seg.x=1550;seg.y=220;\nseg.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL';seg.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED';seg.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';seg.resize(343,36);\nseg.paddingLeft=3;seg.paddingRight=3;seg.paddingTop=3;seg.paddingBottom=3;seg.itemSpacing=0;\nseg.fills=[solid(C.track)];seg.cornerRadius=10;\nconst items=[['Bills',false],['Payments',false],['Subscription',true]];\nfor(const [label,active] of items){\n  const it=stack('HORIZONTAL',0,{hugP:false,hugC:false});it.name='Segment / '+label;\n  it.layoutGrow=1;it.primaryAxisAlignItems='CENTER';it.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';it.cornerRadius=8;\n  if(active){it.fills=[solid(C.surface)];it.effects=[{type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.1,g:0.1,b:0.15,a:0.12},offset:{x:0,y:1},radius:3,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'}];}\n  it.appendChild(txt(label,13,active?'SemiBold':'Medium',active?C.brand:C.ink2));\n  seg.appendChild(it);\n}\n```\nSegment height: seg fixed 36 padding 3 → children stretched? counterAxisAlignItems of seg default 'MIN' → children height hug (text 18) not filling 30. Set seg.counterAxisAlignItems='STRETCH' → children full height 30. But then each `it` needs counterAxisSizingMode? STRETCH handles it. Set stack hugC? If parent stretches, child height forced. OK: seg.counterAxisAlignItems='STRETCH'. But helper default align MIN; pass align:'STRETCH'.\n\nHmm careful: 'STRETCH' valid for counterAxisAlignItems ✓.\n\nAlso text inside `it` centered ✓.\n\nReturn {tb:tb.id,hd:hd.id,seg:seg.id}.\n\nAlso store globally? Subsequent calls can't share JS state. I'll return IDs and read from result. Also set plugin data? Not needed.\n\nLet me also worry: `figma.createComponent()` then setting layoutMode then resize — for components ok.\n\nPotential issue: stack() sets primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED' default with resize only if w/h given... for hug both, no resize — frame sizes to content ✓.\n\nAlso: default clipsContent for frames = true. For stacks fine.\n\nLet me finalize Call 1. Also I want to place components far right: x=1600. y cursor: tb 0..80, hd 120..172, seg 220..256. Next call y from 320.\n\nAlso IMPORTANT: after creating text with fontName set — loaded ✓.\n\nletterSpacing pixels small ok.\n\nNow write Call 1 for real. I'll include a try/catch? No — let errors surface.\n\nOne more: page bg: page.backgrounds default; fine.\n\nAfter Call 1, Call 2 (ItemRow, CategoryCard, BudgetCard, CreditEntry), Call 3 (SubRow, SummaryCard, FactorRow, GaugeCard), then frames.\n\nLet me draft Call 2 details:\n\nItemRow component ('Progress Row'):\n```js\nconst row=figma.createComponent();row.name='Progress Row';row.x=1600;row.y=320;\nrow.layoutMode='VERTICAL';row.itemSpacing=6;row.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO';row.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';row.resize(311,10);\n// RowA\nconst ra=stack('HORIZONTAL',8,{align:'CENTER'});ra.name='Top';ra.layoutGrow=1; // hmm child of vertical parent: grow = height grow. Don't grow; hug height.\n```\nIn vertical parent, children width: counterAxisAlignItems='STRETCH' on row → children stretch width. Set row.counterAxisAlignItems='STRETCH'. Then ra hug height, width fill.\nra: name text grow: name.layoutGrow=1; amount text.\n```js\nconst name=txt('Auto & transport',13,'Medium',C.ink,{name:'Name'});name.layoutGrow=1;\nconst amount=txt('$350',13,'SemiBold',C.ink,{name:'Amount'});\nra.appendChild(name);ra.appendChild(amount);\n// RowB\nconst rb=stack('HORIZONTAL',8,{align:'CENTER'});rb.name='Bottom';\nconst tr=figma.createFrame();tr.name='Track';tr.layoutGrow=1;tr.resize(200,5);tr.cornerRadius=2.5;tr.fills=[solid(C.track)];tr.clipsContent=false;\nconst fillR=figma.createRectangle();fillR.name='Fill';fillR.resize(130,5);fillR.cornerRadius=2.5;fillR.fills=[solid(C.auto)];tr.appendChild(fillR);\nrb.appendChild(tr);\nconst left=txt('Left $186',11,'Regular',C.ink3,{name:'Left'});\nrb.appendChild(left);\nrow.appendChild(ra);row.appendChild(rb);\n```\nWait: tr as child of horizontal stack with layoutGrow=1 → fills width; height 5; rb counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER' centers track & text vertically. tr is plain frame (no layout) with child rect at 0,0 ✓. Track resize(200,5): in stack, layoutGrow overrides width; height fixed 5 ✓. But careful: plain frame in auto-layout with layoutGrow: width from parent; height from resize ✓.\n\nfillR default width 130 = 0.653*199? track width will be 311 - leftWidth - 8. leftWidth \"Left $186\" at 11px ≈ 52 → track ≈ 251. Fill default set later precisely? In component, set fill width = round(0.653*251)=164. But track.width in component after layout... I'll set fill width after