n\nFrame 02 assembly:\n```js\ncontent stack gap 14:\n seg instance (343)\n summary instance\n rows: subRowComp.createInstance() ×4 with overrides:\n   row1 default Patreon ✓ (no overrides).\n   row2: name 'Netflix', price '$12/mo', logo swap Netflix: const lg=rowInst.findOne(n=>n.name==='Logo'); lg.swapComponent(netflixComp); lg.rescale(0.75);\n   row3: 'Apple payment','$19.99/mo', Apple.\n   row4: 'Spotify','$6.99/mo', Spotify.\n```\nSubRow component: default name 'Patreon membership', price '$19.99/mo', logo Patreon 0.75.\n\nFrame 03 assembly:\n```\n header: title 'Credit Score', plus hidden\n content stack gap 14:\n  gauge instance\n  factors header: 'Factors' 17 Bold (grow spacer)\n  factorRow instances ×3:\n   r1 default ✓\n   r2: Name 'Credit Utilization', Value '95%', Detail '-15%', Rating 'Not bad', chip fill warnTint, rating text color warn.\n   r3: Name 'Age of credit', Value '8 years', Detail '' , Rating 'Good' (default colors).\n```\nWait factor data: \"Credit Utilization · 95% · Not bad · -15%\" — detail '-15%'. Hmm \"95%\" for utilization seems odd but data is fixed — use verbatim.\n\nNote Age of credit detail empty → set characters '' — text node with 0 chars might have errors? Setting characters='' is allowed (empty text). Height may collapse; gap stays. Fine.\n\nPrototype Call 7:\n```js\nasync function hotspot(frame,overNode,destId,label){\n  const fb=frame.absoluteBoundingBox;const ob=overNode.absoluteBoundingBox;\n  const r=figma.createRectangle();r.name='Hotspot · '+label;r.resize(Math.round(ob.width),Math.round(ob.height));\n  frame.appendChild(r);\n  r.x=Math.round(ob.x-fb.x);r.y=Math.round(ob.y-fb.y);\n  r.fills=[solid('#FFFFFF',0)];\n  r.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:destId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:0.3,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}];\n  return r;\n}\n```\nEasing 'EASE_OUT' — I believe valid. Wrap in try: if throws, set without transition: reactions=[{action:{type:'NOD