{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 4 components created:\n- Subscription Row: 11:30 (h68)\n- Subscription Summary Card: 11:43 (h101)\n- Factor Row: 11:46 (h64)\n- Credit Gauge Card: 11:54 (h204)\n\nNow assemble 01_Expenses frame. Content budget: 636px height (y96 to y732).\nChildren: BudgetCard 177, Categories header ~22, AutoCard 148, BillCard ~192 (row3 visible), CreditCard 60. Sum = 599. Gaps 4×g + top padding 8. 636-8-599 = 29 → gap = 7. Tight but fits. If over, reduce.\n\nLet me write the assembly call for 01_Expenses with all overrides and the fit logic.\n\nCode plan:\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('4:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfonts...\nhelpers C,hex,solid,txt,stack,recolor,findNode,setRow\nconst IDS = {status:'1:25',home:'1:35',tabbar:'8:2',header:'8:22',seg:'8:29',prow:'10:11',cat:'10:19',budget:'10:52',credit:'10:66',subrow:'11:30',subsum:'11:43',factor:'11:46',gauge:'11:54', sb:'4:2'};\nICONS map with More:'2:7' etc.\n\nconst f=figma.createFrame(); f.name='01_Expenses'; f.x=0;f.y=0; f.resize(375,812); f.fills=[solid(C.bg)]; f.clipsContent=true; f.cornerRadius=0;\n\nconst sb=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:25')).createInstance(); sb.x=0;sb.y=0; f.appendChild(sb);\nconst hd=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('8:22')).createInstance(); hd.x=0;hd.y=44; f.appendChild(hd); // title default 'Expenses'\nconst tb=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('8:2')).createInstance(); tb.x=0;tb.y=732; f.appendChild(tb);\nconst hi=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('1:35')).createInstance(); hi.x=0;hi.y=778; f.appendChild(hi);\n\nconst ct=stack('VERTICAL',10,{}); ct.name='Content'; ct.x=0;ct.y=96; ct.resize(375,636);\nct.paddingTop=8;ct.paddingBottom=0;ct.paddingLeft=16;ct.paddingRight=16;\nct.primaryAxisSizingMode='FIXED'; ct.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';\nf.appendChild(ct);\n\nconst bc=(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('10:52')).createInstance(); bc.layoutAlign='STRETCH'? \n```\n\nWait — content children width 343 = 375-32 ✓. Use layoutAlign='STRETCH' so they fill.\n\nCategories header: hstack, layoutAlign='STRETCH', gap 8, align CENTER: 'Categories' 17 Bold layoutGrow=1 + Icon_More 22 ink2.\n\nAuto card instance: default.\n\nBill card: overrides as planned.\n\nCredit card instance default.\n\nThen fit: measure ct.height? Content is FIXED 636 so height stays 636; overflow means children clipped. Instead measure sum of children heights + gaps:\nsum = bc.height + catHead.height + auto.height + bill.height + cc.height\navail = 636 - 8 (padding) - sum\ngap = Math.floor(avail/4); clamp [6,10]. If avail < 24 → gap 6 and maybe shrink.\n\nIf gap computed <6, apply mitigation: bc '$738' fontSize → 30; bc padding 12; re-measure.\n\nActually simpler and robust: set gap = Math.max(6, Math.min(10, Math.floor(avail/4))). If still overflow (gap 6 and avail<24), reduce LeftAmount font size to 30 and bc paddings to 12, recompute avail, set gap again. Since I can override instance properties.\n\nEstimated heights: bc 177, catHead ~24 (17 Bold line ~22 + nothing) ≈22, auto 148, bill 192, cc 60 → 599. avail=29 → gap=7. Fine, no mitigation needed likely.\n\nsetRow implementation (same as Call 6):\n```js\nfunction setRow(ri,nameT,amountT,leftT,frac,colorHex,leftHex){\n  const nameN=findNode(ri,'Name');const amN=findNode(ri,'Amount');const lfN=findNode(ri,'Left');const tk=findNode(ri,'Track');const fl=findNode(ri,'Fill');\n  const issues=[];\n  if(!nameN)issues.push('no Name');else nameN.characters=nameT;\n  if(!amN)issues.push('no Amount');else amN.characters=amountT;\n  if(!lfN)issues.push('no Left');else{lfN.characters=leftT;lfN.fills=[solid(leftHex||C.ink3)];}\n  if(!tk)issues.push('no Track');\n  if(!fl)issues.push('no Fill');\n  if(tk&&fl){fl.fills=[solid(colorHex)];fl.resize(Math.max(6,Math.round(frac*(tk.width>10?tk.width:251))),5);}\n  return issues;\n}\n```\n\nBill overrides:\n```js\nconst bill=...createInstance; \nconst t=findNode(bill,'Title'); t.characters='Bill & Utilities';\nconst tot=findNode(bill,'Total'); tot.characters='$320';\nconst tile=findNode(bill,'Tile'); tile.fills=[solid(C.warnTint)];\nconst ic=findNode(bill,'Icon_Car'); await ic.swapComponent(await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2:3')); ic.name='Icon_Bill'; recolor(ic,C.warn);\nconst r1=findNode(bill,'Row 1'),r2=findNode(bill,'Row 2'),r3=findNode(bill,'Row 3');\nsetRow(r1,'Subscriptions','$52','Left $0',1,C.warn,C.bad);\nsetRow(r2,'House service','$138','Left $10',0.93,C.warn);\nr3.visible=true;\nsetRow(r3,'Maintenance','$130','Left $30',0.8125,C.warn);\n```\nNote r3 default text already Maintenance but set anyway (visible toggling shouldn't matter).\n\nWait — icons: Icon_Car name — in Category Card component I created icon via icon('Car') which sets name 'Icon_Car'. ✓\n\nswapComponent is async? In plugin API, `swapComponent` is synchronous (returns InstanceNode). Actually `instance.swapComponent(componentNode)` is sync. I'll not await (await on non-promise is fine anyway).\n\nTile: the Tile frame contains the icon? In my Category Card, 'Head' stack: Tile frame (36, radius 11, autoTint) containing Icon_Car instance (auto-sized 20?). Actually I placed icon inside tile? Let me recall: \"'Head' (Tile 36 radius 11 autoTint + Icon_Car auto 20 + Title ... )\" — Tile contains icon, and Title/Total are siblings of Tile. findNode(bill,'Icon_Car') finds it regardless of nesting ✓.\n\nIcon size 20: rescale(20/24) applied in component. After swapComponent, does size change? Swapping keeps instance size (may distort aspect but icons are all 24-based squares). Fine.\n\nCategories header More icon: 22.\n\nCredit card default 'Credit score' '660 · Good · +6pts' ✓.\n\nReturn ids and diagnostics.\n\nOne concern: content children order — appendChild order: bc, catHead, auto, bill, cc.\n\nAnother: Tab Bar instance y=732 — but home indicator y=778 overlaps tab bar (732+80=812; indicator 778..812 inside tab bar area, by design as in iOS ✓).\n\nStatus bar: instance of 1:25 is 375×44 ✓.\n\nAlso need frame-level: nothing else.\n\nFont loading: all DM Sans styles.\n\nText overrides on instances need font loaded ✓.\n\nLet me also double check 'Title' override: header component Title text 'Expenses' default → for 01 no override needed.\n\nNow, one more consideration: `ct.resize(375,636)` then padding — children width via STRETCH = 375-32=343 ✓.\n\ncatHead: stack hug with layoutAlign STRETCH: children: title layoutGrow=1, icon fixed. Height: hugC → tall as tallest child (~22-24).\n\nOK write the call. Keep under 50k chars — fine.\n\nAlso remember: no throwing — wrap risky ops in try/catch collecting issues, return diagnostics.\n\nPotential null: findNode for 'Title' etc. — collect issues.\n\nLet me write it.","signature":"29fec95ec7264b83a15543dd"}],"id":"41467798-d6f7-4ac6-b2de-e1f41905aca6","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"ce31a178-b977-49f3-a276-da0f01d702a1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:53:41.246Z","thinking_duration_ms":47977}
