lude Row 3.\n- auto instance: set its Row 3 visible=false.\n\nAlso height: auto card height will stay 148 after hiding row3 (35+9... wait row height 35 + gap 9 = 44; 148-44=104? Hmm: comp height 148 with Row3 hidden. So visible Row3 adds ~44 → bill height becomes ~192. Good, matches earlier estimate. And gap recalc: sum becomes 550+44=594, avail=636-8-594=34 → gap=8. Fine, itemSpacing override on ct.\n\nAlso check: does setting component child visible=true then bill overrides on Row 3 work? Yes.\n\nSteps in one call:\n1. comp Row3: comp.children find name 'Row 3' → visible=true. (Component edit allowed.)\n2. auto instance 12:98: find Row 3 → visible=false.\n3. bill instance 12:124: find Row 3 → should now exist → setRow Maintenance/$130/Left $30/0.8125/warn (visible stays true).\n4. Recompute gap: measure heights, set ct.itemSpacing.\n5. Return diagnostics incl. bill.height.\n\nNeed setRow + solid + findNode helpers again. Fonts loaded (setting characters on Maintenance row texts).\n\nNote: findNode uses findAll which excludes invisible — but after making Row 3 visible in component, auto's Row 3 is visible=true until we set false; we set visible=false via direct child lookup: auto.children find name. Use children array rather than findAll to be safe (children includes it since visible). After setting visible=false, it stays in children.\n\nLet me write it.","signature":"afbf0d65a3f34cd5924bd611"}],"id":"4eb4d2a7-7d15-48ae-a706-1fd9b9e50fe3","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"cdeffe9a-5fd6-483d-b64a-76679236d434","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:55:31.680Z","thinking_duration_ms":38437}
