{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All three frames assembled:\n- 01_Expenses: 12:37\n- 02_Bill: 15:155\n- 03_Credit_Score: 16:242\n\nNow prototype wiring (Call 7):\n- f01 (12:37): hotspot over Bill card instance (12:124) → 02_Bill (15:155); hotspot over Credit Score Card instance (12:151) → 03_Credit_Score (16:242).\n- f02 (15:155): hotspot over back icon in header → 01_Expenses (12:37); also 'Tab / This Month' tab → 01.\n- f03 (16:242): back icon → 01; This Month tab → 01.\n\nHotspot approach: create rectangle with fills=[], or fill opacity 0. `figma.createRectangle()` with fills=[] — clickable in prototype? Yes, fill-less nodes are still clickable hotspots (Figma prototyping uses node bounds). Common practice: rectangle with 0 opacity fill. I'll use fills=[solid white, opacity 0]... Actually fills=[] works fine for hotspots. But to be safe (some versions require a fill for hit area?), standard is empty fill works. I'll use opacity 0 fill.\n\nPositioning: hotspot must be a child of the frame, positioned over the target. Since frames use absolute positioning for status/header/tab (children of frame directly), but content children are inside auto-layout 'Content'. Adding a hotspot INSIDE auto-layout would disturb layout — so append hotspot to the top frame f and set absolute position via x/y computed from target.absoluteBoundingBox minus frame.absoluteBoundingBox.\n\nBut hotspots appended as children of an auto-layout frame get laid out! f (01_Expenses) is NOT auto-layout (plain frame) ✓. So hotspots as direct children of f with absolute coords = fine.\n\nCompute: const fb=f.absoluteBoundingBox; const bb=target.absoluteBoundingBox; h.x=bb.x-fb.x; h.y=bb.y-fb.y; h.resize(bb.width,bb.height).\n\nOrder: hotspots must render ABOVE the card (z-order top). appendChild puts on top ✓.\n\nReactions:\n```js\nfunction nav(node,destId){\n  try{node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:destId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:300,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}];}\n  catch(e){node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:destId,navigation:'NAVIGATE'},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}];}\n}\n```\nNote duration in ms? Plugin API Transition: {type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration: number (seconds? ms?)}. In plugin API, duration is in milliseconds... Actually figma.Transition duration is in ms (e.g., 300)? Documentation: `duration: number` — \"The duration of the transition in milliseconds\". Hmm, I recall it's ms. Earlier summary said duration:0.3. Let me use 300 (ms) — if invalid it throws and falls back. Actually some APIs use seconds. To be safe, try 300, fallback no transition. Hmm — if 300 were interpreted as seconds that'd be 5 minutes. I believe plugin API uses ms (docs: duration in ms). Yes, figma plugin API Transition.duration is in milliseconds.\n\nBack icon: findNode(hd,'Icon_Back') — it's an instance inside header instance. Setting reactions on a nested instance node: allowed? Reactions on instance children... you can set reactions on nodes inside instances? Overriding interactions inside instances is supported in UI (\"interactions\" propagate from main component; overriding on instance subnodes may not be settable via API — setting `reactions` on instance subnode might throw). Safer: put hotspot rectangle over the back button area instead. Hotspot rect over top-left 56×52 region of header → navigate back. I'll do that: rect at (0,44) size 56×52 in f02/f03.\n\nAlso Tab 'This Month' on 02/03 → 01: hotspot over the This Month tab region. Tab bar 375 wide, 4 tabs. This Month tab x roughly 375*0.5..0.75? Tab order: Overview, This Month, Offers, Setting with SPACE_BETWEEN padding 30. Simpler: hotspot over tab bar region from x≈140 to 260, y 732..812? The This Month tab is second of four: with padding 30, four tabs each ~46 wide? Tab widths are hug (icon+label). Rather than compute, put hotspot over whole tab bar? Then clicking anywhere in tab bar goes to 01 — acceptable but crude; clicking Overview would also navigate (fine, Overview→01? Actually Overview isn't wired; brief only requires listed links). The brief's required links: Bill card→02, back→01, Credit card→03 (entry choice). Tab link optional. I'll add a hotspot over the This Month tab area only: tab bar children — I can read the instance children positions: tb.children (tabs are frames 'Tab / This Month'). absoluteBoundingBox works on them. So hotspot positioned exactly over that child. \n\nFor f01's hotspots: over bill card (12:124) and credit card (12:151) instances.\n\nAlso add back hotspots. Also maybe wire tab This Month on 01 → nothing (already current). Skip.\n\nAlso: brief says \"Header back(Icon_Back)\" on 01 — back on 01 not required to link anywhere.\n\nTotal hotspots:\n- f01: 2 (bill card → 15:155; credit card → 16:242)\n- f02: back (0,44,56,52) → 12:37; This Month tab → 12:37\n- f03: back → 12:37; This Month tab → 12:37\n\nHotspot naming: 'Hotspot / ...'.\n\nAlso need to make sure hotspot rectangles don't block card visuals — fill opacity 0, and they're on top; in presentation only interactions matter.\n\nLet me also set f01 hotspots z-top AFTER everything (they're last appended) ✓.\n\nOne catch: reading absoluteBoundingBox right after creation in same call — layout is computed synchronously on access, should be fine.\n\nWrite Call 7.","signature":"02c7a459266649eea66cb0db"}],"id":"dbc3aaa8-4476-495c-a81a-f9c7d702114f","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"c1f73ee6-f20f-472e-b533-0ac0c6c74ab3","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:58:02.543Z","thinking_duration_ms":40964}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reasoning summary: 三个屏全部组装完毕（01=12:37、02=15:155、03=16:242，均无问题）。现在做原型连线：01 上 Bill 卡→02、Credit Score 卡→03 的隐形热区；02/03 上返回按钮区域和 This Month 标签→01，用 SMART_ANIMATE 导航，失败则降级为无过渡。"}],"id":"dbc3aaa8-4476-495c-a81a-f9c7d702114f","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"b8c8b14f-921f-407c-bb5e-2affa7a427ab","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:58:04.966Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_51d983269026410180923540","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const issues=[];\nfunction solidO(){return {type:'SOLID',color:{r:1,g:1,b:1},opacity:0};}\nfunction nav(node,destId){\n  try{node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:destId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:300,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}];}\n  catch(e){try{node.reactions=[{action:{type:'NODE',destinationId:destId,navigation:'NAVIGATE'},trigger:{type:'CLICK'}}];}catch(e2){issues.push('react:'+e2.message);}}\n}\nfunction hotspot(parent,target,destId,name){\n  const fb=parent.absoluteBoundingBox;\n  let bb;\n  if(target.absoluteBoundingBox){bb=target.absoluteBoundingBox;}else{issues.push('no bbox '+name);return null;}\n  const h=figma.createRectangle();h.name=name;h.fills=[solidO()];\n  h.resize(Math.max(24,bb.width),Math.max(24,bb.height));\n  parent.appendChild(h);\n  h.x=bb.x-fb.x;h.y=bb.y-fb.y;\n  nav(h,destId);\n  return h.id;\n}\nconst f01=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('12:37');\nconst f02=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('15:155');\nconst f03=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('16:242');\n// 01: bill card -> 02, credit card -> 03\nconst billCard=f01.children.find(function(c){return c.name==='Content';}).children.find(function(c){return c.type==='INSTANCE'&&c.name==='Category Card'&&c.id.indexOf('12:124')===0;});\nconst ct01=f01.children.find(function(c){return c.name==='Content';});\nconst billI=ct01.children[3];const credI=ct01.children[4];\nconst h1=hotspot(f01,billI,'15:155','Hotspot / To Bill');\nconst h2=hotspot(f01,credI,'16:242','Hotspot / To Credit Score');\n// 02/03: back area + This Month tab -> 01\nfunction backAndTab(f){\n  const b=figma.createRectangle();b.name='Hotspot / Back';b.fills=[solidO()];b.resize(56,52);\n  f.appendChild(b);b.x=0;b.y=44;nav(b,'12:37');\n  const tb=f.children.find(function(c){return c.name==='Tab Bar';});\n  const tm=tb.children.find(function(c){return c.name==='Tab / This Month';});\n  const h=hotspot(f,tm,'12:37','Hotspot / Tab This Month');\n  return {back:b.id,tab:h};\n}\nconst r2=backAndTab(f02);\nconst r3=backAndTab(f03);\nreturn {h1:h1,h2:h2,f02:r2,f03:r3,issues:issues};","description":"Add prototype hotspots and navigation reactions between the three frames","fileKey":"Lpmrb2cZGL1jkibhtHwaxj"}}],"id":"dbc3aaa8-4476-495c-a81a-f9c7d702114f","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"79379a74-32b6-4a52-9124-f2957e87b294","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:58:17.113Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"call_51d983269026410180923540","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
