{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 6 hotspots were created (ids returned: h1 17:145, h2 17:146, f02 back 17:147 tab 17:183, f03 back 17:184 tab 17:219) but ALL reactions failed — both attempts. The API schema differs from what I used:\n\nFrom the validation error:\n- action.type must be... it lists CONDITIONAL, BACK/CLOSE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME, SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE — no plain 'NODE'?? Hmm, interesting: the error says `Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE'` for one variant — that's the \"action\" variant without navigation? TheNavigateAction should be type:'NODE' with destinationId + navigation. But error says unrecognized keys 'destinationId','navigation'... weird.\n\nWait, actually the error message lists variants it tried. For the second variant: \"Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE' at [0].action.type\" — that suggests this schema variant only accepts BACK|CLOSE for type... This looks like the schema doesn't include the NavigateAction variant?! That can't be right.\n\nHmm, maybe the correct current format uses different field names. Current Figma Plugin API (2024+): `figma.NavigateAction`? Let me recall: PrototypeAction types: \n- NavigateAction: {type: 'NODE', destinationId: string, navigation: 'NAVIGATE'|'SWAP'|'OVERLAY'|'CHANGE_TO', transition?: ...}\n- BackAction: {type:'BACK'}\n- CloseAction: {type:'CLOSE'}\n- urlAction: {type:'URL', url}\n- conditionalAction {type:'CONDITIONAL', conditionalBlocks:[...]}\n- setVariableAction {type:'SET_VARIABLE', variableId, ...}\n- setVariableModeAction {type:'SET_VARIABLE_MODE', variableCollectionId, variableModeId}\n\nTrigger types: {type:'CLICK'} should be valid (\"click\" trigger = {type:'CLICK'}). But error says expected 'ON_CLICK'|'ON_HOVER'|... Hmm! So this schema expects trigger.type 'ON_CLICK'. And the error \"Expected null, received object at [0].trigger\" in one variant...\n\nThis suggests the environment validates against a DIFFERENT schema than standard figma plugin API — possibly a mock/validation layer. The trigger enum: ON_CLICK, ON_HOVER, ON_PRESS, ON_DRAG, ON_MEDIA_END. And action types: CONDITIONAL, BACK, CLOSE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME, SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE... and apparently NODE is rejected?? But then how to navigate?\n\nWait, maybe the NODE action variant requires 'transition' and specific structure, and my transition object was wrong, causing all variants to fail. The error for variant 2 said \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation'\" — that's odd.\n\nHmm, maybe the correct action for navigation in this API version is:\n{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{...}} — that's what I did.\n\nUnless... the schema expects `navigation` values differently and my 'transition' shape broke it, but \"unrecognized keys\" wouldn't appear then.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe there's a dev-tools validation JSON schema that's slightly stale. Let me look at error more carefully:\n\nVariant list for action:\n1. CONDITIONAL + conditionalBlocks\n2. type BACK | CLOSE (no other keys)\n3. URL + url\n4. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME + mediaAction (+navigation?) — \"Unrecognized key(s): 'navigation'\" hmm it says Unrecognized 'navigation' — so variant 4 accepts... weird\n5. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME + mediaAction + amountToSkip\n6. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME + mediaAction + newTimestamp\n7. action.transition missing issues...\n8. SET_VARIABLE + variableId\n9. SET_VARIABLE_MODE + variableCollectionId + variableModeId\n\nNo NODE variant at all! But there's that odd \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following...\" fragment which hints a variant WITH transition exists — probably the NODE variant got mis-validated because destinationId/navigation are unrecognized → meaning in THIS schema, navigate action might be expressed differently.\n\nHold on — maybe in this environment (Figma's actual current API as of 2025), the navigate action is:\n{type: 'NODE', destinationId: ..., navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: ...} — standard. The validator rejecting it seems wrong...\n\nAlternatively the correct trigger is 'ON_CLICK' — the trigger failure alone would make the whole reactions assignment fail even if action were right. Let me retry with:\n- trigger: {type:'ON_CLICK'}\n- action: {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE', duration:300, easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}\n\nIf action NODE still rejected, try without navigation key, or navigation might be part of... Actually wait, in newer plugin API, NavigateAction: {type: 'NODE', destinationId: string; navigation: 'NAVIGATE' | 'SWAP' | 'OVERLAY' | 'CHANGE_TO'; transition?: ...; transitionDuration?...}. Hmm.\n\nHmm, another thought: maybe transition duration unit issue wouldn't cause \"unrecognized keys\".\n\nActually, maybe the validator is from figma's REST-ish prototype schema where navigate action is:\n{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation} — no transition (transition separate?). The error variant list just doesn't show the NODE variant message because... it showed fragments: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following...\" — that fragment appears twice nested weirdly: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched: Required value missing at [0].action.transition\" — meaning one variant REQUIRES transition and my transition failed its inner validation! That's the NODE/NAVIGATE variant!\n\nSo the NODE variant exists but its inner keys failed. Why? If transition inner schema failed, the error should detail transition issues. The nested fragment is truncated/odd.\n\nPlan: try variations systematically in one call, testing on a single node with try/catch, returning which variant worked:\nV1: trigger ON_CLICK + action {type:'NODE',destinationId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:300,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}\nV2: same but duration 0.3\nV3: same but transition