sport $350\" there's the teal bar, and strikethrough-looking \"Left $186\" text is positioned ON the bar row. So the Bottom frame is likely h≈11 but Track has layoutGrow and fills height? The Track is h5 but might have stretched? The text sits on same line as bar → they're horizontal siblings but the text starts near x=0? No — the text appears to START at the left edge and the bar overlays it. Possibly the Bottom stack has counterAxisAlignItems CENTER and both children overlap because... they can't overlap in auto-layout.\n\nHmm, actually maybe the issue: the 'Left' text in the row has layoutAlign STRETCH? Or the Track grew to full width and the Left text wrapped below into the bar's space? Let me look more carefully: \"Left $186\" appears at left edge, with the teal bar drawn over/through it. The bar spans most of the width. If Bottom = [Track(layoutGrow), Left], the Left text would be at the RIGHT side. But it's at LEFT and overlapped...\n\nAlternative explanation: the Bottom stack direction is VERTICAL (my Call 6 spec may have made Bottom a vertical stack? no...). Or the row's Bottom frame contains Track and Left as children but the Track's Fill rectangle (child of Track) has absolute positioning? The Fill is inside Track (a frame). If Track frame has clipping off and Fill rect is bigger than track... Fill h5 w=frac*track. Fine.\n\nActually — here's a likely cause: In the Progress Row component, maybe I set the Track as a frame with layoutGrow=1 but the Bottom stack's primary axis sizing FIXED width 311... and 'Left' text also layoutGrow? Can't tell without inspecting. Simplest: inspect one Progress Row in the Auto card to see actual layout, then fix.\n\nActually wait, look at Bill card rows: \"Left $0\" strikethrough-ish under Subscriptions, similarly overlapped by orange bar. And \"Left $10\", \"Left $30\". All rows show the Left text vertically centered ON the bar line. So the Bottom stack probably is: horizontal [Track, Left] BUT the text has width 0? No, text is visible...\n\nHmm, they overlap → not auto-layout siblings. Unless the 'Left' text was placed INSIDE the Track frame as absolute-positioned child at x=0? Or the Bottom frame isn't auto-layout at all and children positioned manually overlapping.\n\nWhatever the cause, the fix: make row Bottom a proper horizontal auto-layout [Track(grow), Left text] OR vertical [Track, Left] stacked. The original design intent (from my plan): \"Bottom (Track + Left text)\" — display bar and \"Left $186\" beneath or beside. In the reference benchmark design (typical), each item row shows name, amount, progress bar, and \"Left $x\" below the bar. The current render puts text on the bar line at left — looks like a bug.\n\nLet me inspect the Progress Row component structure (10:11) read-only.\n\n**Other observations:**\n\n02_Bill: looks great. Patreon logo tile white circle ✓, Netflix ✓, Apple ✓, Spotify ✓. Segmented control ✓. Summary card ✓. One nit: bottom area is empty (content ends ~570) — acceptable. Header plus icon present ✓ (brief: Header back \"Bill\" add ✓).\n\n03_Credit_Score: gauge looks great! 660, Good chip, +6pts, 400/850, Last update ✓. Factors ✓ (95% Good / 95% Not bad warn / 8 years Good). \"Age of credit\" has no detail line — ✓ per data. Nit: rows 2 and 3 have taller left blocks due to detail text; fine. The gauge arc ends at ~58% — ✓.\n\n01 nit: budget card \"Monthly budget$2,550\" — missing space? Bottom row: 'Monthly budget' text + '$2,550' — screenshot shows \"Monthly budget$2,550\" very close. There's a gap but small (grow + right aligned). It's \"Monthly budget\" then \"$2,550\" — looks tight but okay. Actually screenshot shows them adjacent with no visible gap: \"Monthly budget$2,550\". The BottomRow has grow on label and amount at right end — since card width 343-28 padding=315, \"Monthly budget\" ~85px, \"$2,550\" at right edge. But screenshot shows them adjacent near center-left?? Wait no — looking again: \"Monthly budget$2,550\" appears at left side. Hmm, the BottomRow: 'Monthly budget' 12 Regular (layoutGrow=1) + '$2,550' 14 SemiBold. If grow applied, $2,550 should be at far right. In screenshot, both are at left, adjacent. So layoutGrow on 'Monthly budget' may not have been set, and BottomRow is hug width? Or BottomRow fixed but dist MIN. It reads \"Monthly budget$2,550\" — indeed no gap. Minor polish: set label layoutGrow=1 so amount right-aligns.\n\nAlso budget card: \"total spent $1,812\" chip row — ✓.\n\nAlso progress bar in budget card: fill 71% ✓.\n\nAlso the Auto card icon tile: light teal bg with car ✓. Bill card: warnTint tile with bill icon (orange) ✓.\n\nTab bar ✓ (This Month active purple, others gray). Home indicator ✓ (black bar at bottom).\n\nSo fixes needed:\n1. Progress Row 'Left' text overlapping track — inspect and fix layout in component (fix propagates to all instances, but text overrides remain).\n2. Budget card bottom row: right-align $2,550 (set 'Monthly budget' layoutGrow=1 in component 10:52).\n\nLet me inspect Progress Row component first.","signature":"aaea8572d83b42088b6dc598"}],"id":"ec05c23d-c066-40ff-aab4-e61eb2f70aa1","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"b45aabaf-24ff-42f4-bf8f-785411d85851","timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:01:43.832Z","thinking_duration_ms":56669}
