{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed: fresh read showed prW=311, sizing FIXED both, botAlign STRETCH — yet botW was STILL 100 with botSizing AUTO/AUTO. So `layoutAlign='STRETCH'` genuinely doesn't stretch when the child's own sizing is AUTO in this environment. After force-setting bot.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize(311), after read shows botW=311, trkW=256 ✓ and setRow re-applied with correct widths.\n\nWait — but \"after\" values: are those flushed? They were read after mutation in the SAME execution... trkW 256 after forcing — could also be stale? No: 256 = 311-47-8, computed AFTER the resize — plausible fresh. Hmm, inconsistent with the earlier \"stale read\" theory. Whatever — the important part: the component now has Bottom 311 wide, Track 256. The setRow calls used tk.width — if tk.width was stale 45 at that moment, fills are wrong again! Order in this call: force-resize FIRST, then setRow. trk.width read inside setRow returned... \"after.trkW\"=256 was read after setRow. If setRow saw 45, fills = frac*45. If it saw 256, correct.\n\nUgh, uncertainty. Solution: verify via screenshot of 01 — the fastest reliable check. Also budget BottomRow: bc counter FIXED set last call — but did BottomRow stretch? Same issue may apply (BottomRow sizing AUTO + STRETCH not working). Need same force: find Budget BottomRow, set counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize(311,18)? For horizontal AL (BottomRow horizontal), width = PRIMARY axis! primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED + resize(311,h). Then grow on 'Monthly budget' pushes $2,550 right.\n\nSimilarly Top frame in Progress Row: Top alignSTRETCH, sizing AUTO/AUTO, w145 → same problem: amount not right-aligned (visible in screenshot: amounts adjacent to names). Force: Top counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' (vertical parent → width is counter) + resize(311,17). Hmm wait Top is horizontal AL, its parent vertical → Top width = counter axis of parent → child's counterAxisSizingMode... For a child in vertical parent: child's width controlled by child.counterAxisSizingMode + layoutAlign. Set counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize(311,17). Inside Top: Name grow1 → pushes Amount right ✓.\n\nAlso TopRow in Budget card: hug is fine (design: chip + total spent adjacent, left-aligned).\n\nAlso check Category Card Head: title grow + total right? Head w? In screenshot \"$600\" sits right after title... Actually screenshot shows \"Auto & transport  $600\" adjacent-ish with gap — hmm, Head: Tile+icon+Title(grow)+Total. If Head is hug width, total adjacent. In screenshot 01, \"$600\" appears mid-card, right after title with ~10px gap — looks like hug. Design-wise, total should be right-aligned at card edge. Let me check Head frame: if alignSTRETCH + AUTO sizing — same fix: Head counterAxisSizingMode FIXED + resize(311,36)? Head is horizontal, parent (Category Card) vertical, content width 311 → Head w311.\n\nAnd Credit Score Card + Subscription Row: SPACE_BETWEEN dist with FIXED primary? Subscription Row primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED (343) → SPACE_BETWEEN works ✓ (screenshot 02 shows chevron right-aligned ✓). Factor Row: FIXED 343 SPACE_BETWEEN ✓ (screenshot 03 shows right-aligned values ✓). Credit Score Card 10:66 SPACE_BETWEEN — screenshot 01 shows chevron at right ✓.\n\nSegmented Control segments STRETCH worked (screenshot) because parent FIXED.\n\nSo remaining fixes:\n1. Progress Row Top → FIXED width 311.\n2. Budget Card BottomRow → FIXED width 311 (primary axis).\n3. Category Card Head → check and force FIXED 311.\n\nCategory Card Head: horizontal AL inside Category Card (vertical). Width = counter axis → set Head.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize(311, h).\n\nThen re-run setRow (fills may be stale-based), and re-screenshot 01.\n\nLet me do all in one call, then screenshot 01 to verify everything visually.","signature":"0d8b631f757244f6ad579ab2"}],"id":"feb6e453-e4db-42c0-8f28-4946c8009b64","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_se