{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   User request (Chinese): 在 Figma 文件 https://www.figma.com/design/Lpmrb2cZGL1jkibhtHwaxj/ 中完成完整设计——先读「00·Start Here」设计任务，参考「01·Foundations」视觉规范，复用「02·Components」组件，使用「04·Media」素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。\n\n   Benchmark constraints (system prompt): Use ONLY assigned file (fileKey `Lpmrb2cZGL1jkibhtHwaxj`); whoami already confirmed account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai; preserve all reference pages and their nodes; create the complete design inside 03 · Workspace (page 4:2, was empty); new frames/components/prototype connections allowed there; do NOT replace reference pages, create a different file, or switch accounts; use supplied Figma tools directly without delegating; load fonts before editing text; build in manageable sections; add prototype interactions required by brief; inspect screenshots of all required screens and fix visible problems (multiple fix+recheck cycles allowed); finish with the assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations; do not claim completion for unfinished work. Unattended session — resolve routine choices from the brief without waiting. BEFORE EVERY TOOL CALL include a concise decision summary prefixed exactly 'Reasoning summary:'; final response must have 'Reasoning summary: ...' on the first line, then 'Final answer:' and the answer.\n\n   Brief requirements (from 00 · Start Here, read earlier): 3 frames named exactly **01_Expenses**, **02_Bill**, **03_Credit_Score** (375×812 mobile), wired as clickable prototype. Fixed data verbatim: September 2020 · total spent $1,812; Left to spend $738 · Monthly budget $2,550; Auto & transport · $600 (Icon_Car) → items Auto & transport $350/Left $186, Auto insurance $250/Left $120; Bill & Utilities · $320 (Icon_Bill) → items Subscriptions $52/Left $0, House service $138/Left $10, Maintenance $130/Left $30; 02 subscriptions: Patreon membership $19.99/mo, Netflix $12/mo, Apple payment $19.99/mo, Spotify $6.99/mo; Summary 'Your monthly payment for subscriptions' $58.97; Credit: 660 Good +6pts, range 400–850, Last update on 20 Jul 2020; Factors: On-time payments 95%/Good/1 missed, Credit Utilization 95%/Not bad/-15%, Age of credit 8 years/Good. Links: Bill card → 02_Bill; 02 back → 01_Expenses; 03 back → 01_Expenses; 03 entry point = my choice (Credit Score Card on 01). Tab bar Overview/This Month/Offers/Setting with This Month active on all screens.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (code ≤50000 chars, getNodeByIdAsync, setCurrentPageAsync)\n   - ATOMIC CALLS: any thrown error rolls back ALL changes from that use_figma call (verified 3×) — never let a call throw; collect diagnostics instead\n   - **Environment quirk: layoutAlign='STRETCH' is a no-op when the child's own sizing modes are AUTO** — must set child counterAxisSizingMode (or primaryAxisSizingMode for horizontal children) ='FIXED' + explicit resize\n   - **Component width/sizing changes do NOT propagate to already-created instances** — fix shells per-instance\n   - **Invisible component children (visible=false) do NOT materialize in instance .children or findAll** — workaround: make them visible in component, hide per-instance\n   - **layoutGrow only accepts integers in this environment** (floats rejected) — use fixed pixel widths instead\n   - **TEXT nodes have no primaryAxisSizingMode** — use textAutoResize='NONE' + resize(w,h) + textAlignHorizontal for fixed-width text\n   - Prototype reactions valid format: `{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'},actions:[{type:'NODE',destinationId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:300,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}` (trigger 'CLICK' invalid; duration in ms; `action` singular rejected — must be `actions` plural)\n   - Hotspots: rectangles with fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:white,opacity:0}] appended to non-auto-layout top frames, positioned via absoluteBoundingBox deltas\n   - Instance overrides that work: characters, fills, visible, swapComponent, rescale, counterAxisSizingMode/resize on instance children, textAutoResize\n   - Logo swap pattern: `lg.swapComponent(comp)` then `if(lg.width>37) lg.rescale(36/lg.width)`\n   - Icon recoloring via findAll VECTOR nodes and setting strokes; `rescale(size/24)` for icon sizing\n   - Same-execution layout reads may be stale — prefer deterministic constants (e.g., track width 251 = 311−8−52) or fresh executions\n   - Fonts: DM Sans Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold must be loaded before any text edit\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file Lpmrb2cZGL1jkibhtHwaxj** pages: 0:1 (00 · Start Here), 1:2 (01 · Foundations), 1:3 (02 · Components), 1:4 (04 · Media), 4:2 (03 · Workspace — target)\n   - **Media instances used**: Status Bar 1:25 (375×44), Home Indicator 1:35 (375×34); Icons: Back 2:2, Bill 2:3, Car 2:4, Chevron_Down 2:5, Chevron_Right 2:6, More 2:7, Plus 2:10; Logos: Apple 2:13, Netflix 2:14, Patreon 2:15, Spotify 2:16\n   - **Components created on page 4:2 (x1600 zone)**: Tab Bar 8:2 (375×80), Header 8:22 (375×52, children 'Title' text + 'Plus' icon), Segmented Control 8:29 (343×36, Subscription active), Progress Row 10:11 (311×35; Top[Name grow, Amount], Bottom[Track lmNONE grow1 + Fill rect + Left text]), Category Card 10:19 (343, Head[Tile 36 + icon + Title grow + Total]; Row 1/2/3 — Row 3 NOW visible=true by default), Budget Summary Card 10:52 (343×170, brand #6347EB; TopRow[Period Chip + total spent], 'Left to spend', LeftAmount '$738' 34 Bold, Track 311×6 + Fill 221, BottomRow['Monthly budget' grow + '$2,550']), Credit Score Card 10:66 (343×60 SPACE_BETWEEN), **Subscription Row 11:30** (343×68: LogoTile 44 r12 #F4F4F8 + Logo(Patreon rescale 0.75) + Name 14 Medium grow + Price 13 SemiBold + Icon_ChevRight 18 ink3; padding 12/14), **Subscription Summary Card 11:43** (343×101 brand r16: label 13 Medium white.85 + '$58.97' 32 Bold), **Factor Row 11:46** (343×64 SPACE_BETWEEN: left[Name 14 Medium; Detail 12 ink2], right[Value 15 Bold; Chip r999 goodTint w/ Rating 12 SemiBold good]), **Credit Gauge Card 11:54** (343×204: Gauge 200×104 clip [GaugeTrack ellipse arcData {π→2π, innerRadius .82} #ECECF1; GaugeFill {π→π+(260/450)π} #6347EB; Score '660' 44 Bold y38]; RangeRow 200 SPACE_BETWEEN ['400' | Chip Good + '+6pts' good | '850']; Updated 'Last update on 20 Jul 2020')\n   - **Frames assembled**:\n     - **01_Expenses = 12:37** (x0 y0): Status Bar(0,0), Header inst(0,44), Tab Bar(0,732), Home Indicator(0,778), Content stack(0,96,375×636, paddingTop 8, padL/R 16, itemSpacing 9) children: Budget inst 12:78, Categories Header 12:92 ('Categories' 17 Bold grow + Icon_More 22 ink2), Auto card 12:98 (defaults; its Row 3 visible=false), Bill card 12:124 (Title 'Bill & Utilities', Total '$320', Tile warnTint, Icon_Bill swap+recolor warn, rows: Subscriptions $52/Left $0/bad-left/full bar warn, House service $138/Left $10/0.93 warn, Maintenance $130/Left $30/0.8125 warn), Credit card 12:151\n     - **02_Bill = 15:155** (x500): Status Bar, Header Title 'Bill', Tab Bar, Home Indicator, Content (gap 14, top 10): Segmented Control, Subscription Summary, 4 Subscription Rows (Patreon default / Netflix $12/mo / Apple payment $19.99/mo / Spotify $6.99/mo with logo swaps)\n     - **03_Credit_Score = 16:242** (x1000): Status Bar, Header Title 'Credit Score' + Plus hidden, Tab Bar, Home Indicator, Content (gap 12, top 10): Gauge Card, Factors Header, 3 Factor Rows (r2 Credit Utilization 95% /-15%/Not bad warn; r3 Age of credit 8 years/Good/detail '')\n   - **Prototype hotspots (all wired)**: 17:145 (over Bill card 12:124 → 15:155), 17:146 (over Credit card 12:151 → 16:242), 17:147 (02 back rect 56×52 @0,44 → 12:37), 17:183 (02 'Tab / This Month' → 12:37), 17:184 (03 back → 12:37), 17:219 (03 'Tab / This Month' → 12:37)\n   - **Working helpers (reuse verbatim)**:\n     ```js\n     const C={brand:'#6347EB',bg:'#F6F6F9',surface:'#FFFFFF',ink:'#1A1A1F',ink2:'#63636E',ink3:'#9C9CA6',line:'#ECECF1',track:'#EEEFF4',good:'#12A66B',goodTint:'#E1F5EC',warn:'#DD8500',warnTint:'#FBF0DC',bad:'#E5484D',auto:'#12A594',autoTint:'#DFF4F0',tile:'#F4F4F8'};\n     function hex(h){const n=parseInt(h.slice(1),16);return{r:(n>>16&255)/255,g:(n>>8&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255};}\n     function solid(h,o){return{type:'SOLID',color:hex(h),opacity:o===undefined?1:o};}\n     function findNode(root,name){const a=root.findAll(function(n){return n.name===name;});return a.length?a[0]:null;}\n     function recolor(node,color){const vs=node.findAll(function(n){return n.type==='VECTOR';});for(const v of vs){if(v.strokes&&v.strokes.length)v.strokes=[solid(color)];}}\n     const shadow={type:'DROP_SHADOW',color:{r:0.07,g:0.07,b:0.12,a:0.05},offset:{x:0,y:4},radius:14,spread:0,visible:true,blendMode:'NORMAL'};\n     function nav(destId){return [{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'},actions:[{type:'NODE',destinationId:destId,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:300,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}];}\n     ```\n   - **Final row-fix function (last successful call)**:\n     ```js\n     function fixRow(ri,frac,colorHex,leftHex){\n       const out=[];\n       const top=findNode(ri,'Top');const bot=findNode(ri,'Bottom');const tk=findNode(ri,'Track');const fl=findNode(ri,'Fill');const lf=findNode(ri,'Left');\n       if(top){top.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';top.resize(311,top.height);}else out.push('no Top');\n       if(bot){bot.counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED';bot.resize(311,bot.height);bot.counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER';}else out.push('no Bottom');\n       if(tk){tk.clipsContent=true;}else out.push('no Track');\n       if(lf){lf.textAutoResize='NONE';lf.resize(52,lf.height);lf.textAlignHorizontal='RIGHT';if(leftHex)lf.fills=[solid(leftHex)];}else out.push('no Left');\n       if(fl){fl.fills=[solid(colorHex)];fl.resize(Math.round(frac*251),5);}else out.push('no Fill');\n       return out;\n     }\n     // applied to: component 10:11 (0.653, good), a1 (0.653 good), a2 (0.676 good), b1 (1, warn, bad-left), b2 (0.93 warn), b3 (0.8125 warn)\n     // track width constant: 311 − itemSpacing 8 − Left fixed width 52 = 251\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **\"no r3\" when assembling Bill card**: invisible component child (Row 3, visible=false) doesn't materialize in instance children/findAll. Fix: set Row 3 visible=true in component 10:19, set visible=false on Auto instance's Row 3, set overrides on Bill instance's Row 3.\n   - **Reactions schema rejections (all 6 hotspots)**: trigger 'CLICK' → must be 'ON_CLICK'; `{action:...}` singular → \"Please update the `actions` field\"; final working: `{trigger:{type:'ON_CLICK'},actions:[{type:'NODE',...,transition:{type:'SMART_ANIMATE',duration:300,easing:{type:'EASE_OUT'}}}]}`.\n   - **Progress Row overlap (\"Left $…\" struck through by bar)**: Fill rect (164px) overflowed Track (45px, lmNONE) over the Left text. Root causes found incrementally: (a) Bottom/Top hug (w100/w145) because layoutAlign='STRETCH' is ignored when child sizing is AUTO; (b) component sizing changes don't propagate to instances. Fix: per-row force counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' + resize(311) on Top/Bottom.\n   - **Fills stayed 29px after re-running setRow**: instance Track width genuinely 45 (stale/propagation issues); setRow's tk.width read unreliable. Fix: deterministic constants — Left text fixed width 52 (textAutoResize='NONE' + resize(52,h) + textAlignHorizontal='RIGHT'), track = 251 constant, Fill = round(frac·251) → 164/170/251/233/204.\n   - **layoutGrow float rejection**: \"Expected integer, received float\" — environment only allows integer layoutGrow; whole call rolled back. Abandoned grow-based approach.\n   - **primaryAxisSizingMode on TEXT node**: TypeError — TEXT nodes use textAutoResize instead. Fixed with textAutoResize='NONE'.\n   - **Budget card 'Monthly budget$2,550' cramped + amounts/totals not right-aligned**: BottomRow/Top/Head all hug despite STRETCH. Fixed by forcing FIXED sizing + resize(311) on Budget BottomRow (primaryAxisSizingMode since horizontal), Progress Row Top, Category Card Head.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - All 3 screens assembled with correct data, overrides, logo/icon swaps, and right-alignment\n   - Prototype fully wired (6 hotspots, 6 ON_CLICK NAVIGATE reactions with SMART_ANIMATE 300ms EASE_OUT)\n   - Verified via screenshots: 02_Bill and 03_Credit_Score render correctly; 01_Expenses alignment fixed after component surgery; final row-fill fix applied but NOT yet visually re-verified\n   - Content fit: 01 content gap=9 (children 170+22+148+192+60=592 + 4×9 + 8 padding = 636 exact); 02/03 have empty bottom space (acceptable)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/Lpmrb2cZGL1jkibhtHwaxj/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。” (with benchmark constraints summarized in section 1; session continued from compacted context — no new user messages in this segment beyond the continuation instruction)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Screenshot 01_Expenses (12:37) to verify the row fix** (bars should now be 164/170/251/233/204px, Left text right-aligned at 52px column, no overlap); fix any remaining visible problems and re-check\n   - Optionally re-verify 02 (15:155) and 03 (16:242) — they were already verified good and were not touched by the row fix (02's subscription rows and 03 unaffected; only Progress Row/Budget/Category Card changed, which appear only on 01)\n   - **Write final answer** in required format ('Reasoning summary:' first line, then 'Final answer:') containing: assigned file URL https://www.figma.com/design/Lpmrb2cZGL1jkibhtHwaxj/; workspace page ID 4:2; screen IDs (01_Expenses 12:37, 02_Bill 15:155, 03_Credit_Score 16:242); component IDs created (8:2, 8:22, 8:29, 10:11, 10:19, 10:52, 10:66, 11:30, 11:43, 11:46, 11:54); prototype work (6 hotspots + reactions: Bill card→02, Credit card→03, back→01 ×2, This Month tab→01 ×2); limitations (e.g., component-level sizing changes don't propagate to instances so shells were fixed per-instance; segments other than Subscription/Bills/Payments not separately designed; tab bar tabs other than This Month not wired)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just completed the final row-fix use_figma call which returned `{\"done\":true,\"issues\":[]}`. This call applied fixRow() to the Progress Row component (10:11) and all 5 row instances (Auto card rows a1/a2, Bill card rows b1/b2/b3): Top/Bottom forced to FIXED width 311, Bottom counterAxisAlignItems CENTER, Track clipsContent=true, Left text fixed 52px right-aligned, Fill widths set to round(frac×251) with correct colors (good teal for Auto rows, warn orange for Bill rows, bad red 'Left $0' text on Subscriptions row). All prior errors (layoutGrow float, primaryAxisSizingMode on TEXT) were resolved en route. The fix has NOT yet been visually verified by screenshot.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Take a screenshot of 01_Expenses (node 12:37) to visually verify the progress rows now render correctly (bars proportional: Auto & transport ~164px teal, Auto insurance ~170px teal, Subscriptions full 251px orange with red 'Left $0', House service ~233px, Maintenance ~204px; 'Left $…' text right-aligned without overlap; amounts/totals right-aligned). This directly continues the fix-verify loop: the previous screenshot verification found \"唯一残留：进度条 Fill 是用旧轨道宽（45px）算的，所以都很短\" and the deterministic fix was just applied successfully. If the screenshot is clean, proceed immediately to the final answer with 'Reasoning summary:' then 'Final answer:' containing the file URL, page ID 4:2, frame IDs 12:37/15:155/16:242, component IDs, prototype connections, and remaining limitations.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/huangxinyue/bench-runs/10case-rerun2-glm/runs/TEST-013_1793607948953/claude-config/projects/-mnt-afs-huangxinyue-bench-runs-10case-rerun2-glm-workspace/88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fa287b-e3f1-4759-ae42-7b214809a163","uuid":"bf836c80-78b6-4c03-9aa7-02d153e95e34","timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:13:59.643Z","isSynthetic":true}
